          "description": "DCR was defined as the percentage of participants who have a CR (CR: disappearance of all target lesions) or partial response (PR: at least a 30% decrease in the sum of diameters of target lesions) or stable disease (SD: neither sufficient shrinkage to qualify for PR nor sufficient increase to qualify for PD \\[PD: \u226520% increase in the sum of diameters of target lesions and an absolute increase of \u22655 mm. The appearance of one or more new lesions was also considered PD\\]). DCR for participants who had not progressed or died at the time of analysis was to be censored at the date of their last tumor assessment. The DCR as assessed by BICR per RECIST 1.1 is presented. Protocol-specified final analysis for this secondary outcome measure was performed with an analysis data cut-off date of Jul-26-2021.",
          "dispersionType": "95% Confidence Interval",
